Subject: [PATCH] decode kernel path: acceptance beside the absorb, per-rank top-64 records (2 x DGX Spark, both ranks)

On top of 0061 (the bundle-11 tree), bundle 12. Rank 0 copies a round's candidates and records to the host and records
an event before the absorb; the host waits on that event, not on the absorb, so the drafts' acceptance runs while the
absorb does. Each rank's head reduces its vocabulary half to top-64 records (528 bytes a row) and the ranks gather those
instead of the full logits; the host merges the halves with the kernel's own order key (ties to rank 0, NaN flagged as
before). The verify frame carries the record count (kind 12), so a rank on 0061 and a rank on 0062 refuse each other's
frames: deploy both ranks together. CPU-tested with four red copies, source-reviewed, and A/B-checked on the pair twice:
92/92 replies exact against 0061 (research/LOCAL-STACK-20261106.md, "Bundle 12"). Generated with `git diff --binary` in a
checkout of the 0061 tree; `git apply` of it gives the served source file for file (1286 files, sha256-compared).

